1342
00:57:04.680 --> 00:57:07.420
We're going to go in shifts so we don't overwhelm her.

1343
00:57:07.580 --> 00:57:10.600
But Michael is like, no, we're all going together.

1344
00:57:10.600 --> 00:57:12.500
At the same time, I'll drive.

1345
00:57:12.740 --> 00:57:16.280
So Jim and Pam are like, well, we can each take people in our separate cars.

1346
00:57:16.400 --> 00:57:18.180
And Oscar's like, separate cars?

1347
00:57:18.360 --> 00:57:21.380
And Kevin's like, I don't believe it.

1348
00:57:21.660 --> 00:57:22.340
I know.

1349
00:57:22.340 --> 00:57:26.660
Well, then Michael has a talking head, and he says, you know, I have flaws, you know,

1350
00:57:27.220 --> 00:57:28.060
so sue me.

1351
00:57:28.140 --> 00:57:29.440
And he's like, no, no, no, don't sue me.

1352
00:57:29.700 --> 00:57:35.760
But Jenna, there was an alt to this talking head, and it's in the deleted scenes, and

1353
00:57:35.760 --> 00:57:37.020
it made me laugh so hard.

1354
00:57:37.020 --> 00:57:40.680
And it's also in the bloopers, and Steve couldn't get through it.

1355
00:57:40.760 --> 00:57:41.460
He kept laughing.

1356
00:57:42.200 --> 00:57:43.020
What is it?

1357
00:57:43.060 --> 00:57:45.200
Okay, this is it.

1358
00:57:45.280 --> 00:57:48.500
There's one take clearly he got through it, because it's in the deleted scenes.

1359
00:57:49.060 --> 00:57:51.840
He says, I am not a bad guy.

1360
00:57:52.340 --> 00:57:55.540
I am a good guy who runs over women with his car.

1361
00:57:56.640 --> 00:57:59.660
Why am I having such a hard time getting my message across?

1362
00:58:00.720 --> 00:58:02.660
Oh my gosh, that is funny.

1363
00:58:03.180 --> 00:58:05.880
And the way Steve does it is so good.

1364
00:58:06.200 --> 00:58:07.040
That's good.

1365
00:58:07.040 --> 00:58:08.280
I have to go watch that.

1366
00:58:08.320 --> 00:58:09.020
Yeah, you have to.

1367
00:58:09.560 --> 00:58:15.440
Well, we don't find out exactly how they get there, but the entire gang does arrive at the

1368
00:58:15.440 --> 00:58:15.920
hospital.

1369
00:58:16.160 --> 00:58:18.660
Michael has a whole bunch of balloons.

1370
00:58:18.660 --> 00:58:20.740
And the entire gang minus Dwight.

1371
00:58:21.680 --> 00:58:25.700
That's right, because Dwight has gone to take care of Sprinkles.

1372
00:58:27.040 --> 00:58:32.540
Everyone gathers around Meredith's bed, and we talked about this scene with Kate, about

1373
00:58:32.540 --> 00:58:36.940
how Steve improvised crawling on top of her in that one moment.

1374
00:58:36.940 --> 00:58:38.980
He's like trying to give her a hug.

1375
00:58:39.280 --> 00:58:40.460
It's pretty amazing.

1376
00:58:40.780 --> 00:58:41.240
It's pretty great.

1377
00:58:41.240 --> 00:58:46.700
There is a deleted scene from this moment where Creed, as they're exiting, just grabs

1378
00:58:46.700 --> 00:58:52.460
all her meds out of the little plastic cups they're sitting on her tray, and Creed just

1379
00:58:52.460 --> 00:58:53.800
pockets all her meds.

1380
00:58:54.940 --> 00:58:56.140
Of course he does.

1381
00:58:56.860 --> 00:59:01.520
Well, I had a favorite moment from this scene, and I wanted to ask you about it because I think

1382
00:59:01.520 --> 00:59:09.420
maybe you improvised it, when Michael is trying to get Meredith to forgive him, he says that

1383
00:59:09.420 --> 00:59:15.000
she should think about the Bible because it says that forgiveness is next to godliness.

1384
00:59:15.820 --> 00:59:18.660
And you mutter, that's cleanliness.

1385
00:59:18.980 --> 00:59:20.120
I did improvise that.

1386
00:59:21.880 --> 00:59:28.380
Oh, I also wanted to mention in this scene, the nurse, who is an improv person from IO.

1387
00:59:28.380 --> 00:59:30.220
Her name is Sylvia McClure.

1388
00:59:31.100 --> 00:59:34.340
Well, I looked at her IMDb, and I found this very interesting.

1389
00:59:34.980 --> 00:59:40.800
In addition to playing a nurse on The Office, she has also played a doctor on Young and the

1390
00:59:40.800 --> 00:59:46.840
Restless, Dexter and Intelligence, a nurse in Night of the Dead, and a receptionist nurse

1391
00:59:46.840 --> 00:59:47.600
on The Unit.

1392
00:59:48.800 --> 00:59:54.300
So she's played a lot of nurses and doctors, and incidentally, she's also twice been cast

1393
00:59:54.300 --> 00:59:54.800
as a nun.

1394
00:59:55.460 --> 01:00:00.780
That is very interesting, like, sort of a, it's like a weird typecasting.

1395
01:00:01.500 --> 01:00:03.060
Yeah, exactly.

1396
01:00:03.060 --> 01:00:08.300
Well, I used to get a lot of auditions for school teachers and nurses.

1397
01:00:08.640 --> 01:00:10.640
Have you ever played a nurse or doctor?

1398
01:00:11.260 --> 01:00:12.520
Yes, actually.

1399
01:00:12.640 --> 01:00:17.880
I played a pediatric nurse in this movie called The Promotion.

1400
01:00:17.880 --> 01:00:28.780
I played a doctor on an episode of Monk, and I played a sexy nurse briefly in one of our

1401
01:00:28.780 --> 01:00:30.640
Halloween episodes of The Office.

1402
01:00:31.780 --> 01:00:35.700
What were you most often typecast as for auditions?

1403
01:00:36.500 --> 01:00:37.980
Before The Office?

1404
01:00:38.200 --> 01:00:39.700
Before The Office.

1405
01:00:40.040 --> 01:00:40.780
Quirky.

1406
01:00:41.060 --> 01:00:41.860
Quirky gal.

1407
01:00:42.100 --> 01:00:42.760
What's up?

1408
01:00:42.800 --> 01:00:44.500
My quirky, quirky fun neighbor.

1409
01:00:44.560 --> 01:00:45.280
Quirky neighbor.

1410
01:00:45.800 --> 01:00:46.480
Yeah.

1411
01:00:48.400 --> 01:00:55.300
Yeah, I was, I got a lot of just the school teachers, waitresses, and nurses.

1412
01:00:56.340 --> 01:01:01.040
Well, I will tell you, we talked about how hard we laughed in this scene, but 11 minutes,

1413
01:01:01.180 --> 01:01:03.220
22 seconds is when you can see us breaking.

1414
01:01:03.560 --> 01:01:07.660
If you're looking for it, that's when Michael crawls on top of Meredith.

1415
01:01:08.280 --> 01:01:16.800
Well, now we can go back to The Office, and we are going to find Dwight telling Angela some

1416
01:01:16.800 --> 01:01:17.440
bad news.

1417
01:01:17.440 --> 01:01:19.040
And she's anxious to see him.

1418
01:01:19.180 --> 01:01:20.680
She wants to know how it went.

1419
01:01:20.820 --> 01:01:21.740
You can just tell.

1420
01:01:22.160 --> 01:01:23.680
And then he's like, hey, monkey.

1421
01:01:23.840 --> 01:01:24.860
And she's like, any problems?

1422
01:01:25.260 --> 01:01:27.840
Well, you left the TV on, and your cat is dead.

1423
01:01:28.420 --> 01:01:30.800
And my character's like, what?

1424
01:01:31.160 --> 01:01:34.060
And he's like, Sparkles, the white one, is dead.

1425
01:01:34.420 --> 01:01:35.920
Yeah, he gets the name wrong.

1426
01:01:36.120 --> 01:01:36.800
It's bad.

1427
01:01:36.880 --> 01:01:37.600
It is bad.

1428
01:01:37.840 --> 01:01:39.340
This will not end well.

1429
01:01:39.340 --> 01:01:46.300
Angela, you get so very immediately emotional, and not in a funny way.

1430
01:01:46.480 --> 01:01:53.580
Like, this is one of the ways that our show allowed characters to be real people, because

1431
01:01:54.540 --> 01:02:01.640
Angela, the character, really loved her cat, and she is heartbroken, and you see that real

1432
01:02:01.640 --> 01:02:03.400
pain here from your character.

1433
01:02:03.600 --> 01:02:05.720
How did you gear up for this scene?

1434
01:02:05.720 --> 01:02:12.460
Well, Greg told me, he said, you know, Angela Martin, hearing this news will be devastated.

1435
01:02:13.060 --> 01:02:20.640
And I need you to play out the beats of hearing news that kind of destroys you in the moment.

1436
01:02:20.820 --> 01:02:25.580
You know, and I feel like we've all had moments in our lives where we've gotten that phone call

1437
01:02:25.580 --> 01:02:27.820
with some bad news, you know, unfortunately.

1438
01:02:28.280 --> 01:02:35.660
And I just sort of thought about a few of those moments where, you know, at first,

1439
01:02:35.720 --> 01:02:39.720
you're just in total shock, where you're not really sure what you heard.

1440
01:02:40.540 --> 01:02:40.980
Yeah.

1441
01:02:41.120 --> 01:02:44.680
And then it's like someone slaps you in the face with the information.

1442
01:02:45.960 --> 01:02:49.280
And then you're trying to make sense of it, but you can't make sense of it.

1443
01:02:49.880 --> 01:02:52.740
It's the unthinkable, and it doesn't make sense.

1444
01:02:53.040 --> 01:02:55.020
And your body is doing all of that.

1445
01:02:55.300 --> 01:02:56.140
You're in shock.

1446
01:02:56.140 --> 01:02:57.100
You're sad.

1447
01:02:57.540 --> 01:03:01.480
Your body, your mind is trying to make it right, but you can't make it right.

1448
01:03:01.660 --> 01:03:02.740
You can't figure it out.

1449
01:03:02.880 --> 01:03:04.380
You don't understand why it happened.

1450
01:03:04.860 --> 01:03:08.340
And I was just trying to process through all of that.

1451
01:03:08.800 --> 01:03:11.700
And yeah, that's what I did.

1452
01:03:11.860 --> 01:03:14.020
Did you have to do a lot of takes of that scene?

1453
01:03:14.020 --> 01:03:14.660
Do you remember?

1454
01:03:14.980 --> 01:03:15.900
No, I didn't.

1455
01:03:15.900 --> 01:03:17.220
I was thankful for that.

1456
01:03:17.600 --> 01:03:20.400
In the next scene, your character is still crying.

1457
01:03:20.580 --> 01:03:22.500
She's standing at reception with Pam.

1458
01:03:22.500 --> 01:03:26.780
And you look like you've been crying for a long time.

1459
01:03:27.260 --> 01:03:32.520
What did you do to get there, to start the scene in a place like that?

1460
01:03:32.600 --> 01:03:33.740
You know, I'm chatty.

1461
01:03:33.860 --> 01:03:38.640
So my instinct would be, I'm standing by reception with you, would be to be hanging out, you know,

1462
01:03:38.940 --> 01:03:40.100
being part of the bullpen.

1463
01:03:40.100 --> 01:03:45.380
And so one of the things I did was I went around the corner by the elevators by myself in between

1464
01:03:45.380 --> 01:03:47.080
takes, and I did not hang out.

1465
01:03:47.200 --> 01:03:50.340
And I just tried to stay in sort of that sad space.

1466
01:03:51.860 --> 01:03:59.540
And also the makeup department, they wanted my eyes to really look like I had bawled my eyes out.

1467
01:03:59.620 --> 01:04:00.560
And they did.

1468
01:04:00.560 --> 01:04:04.000
So I had to get myself back in that emotional place and get sad again.

1469
01:04:04.580 --> 01:04:11.240
And also the makeup department, Kenneth Paul, who did my makeup, did like this type of eyeliner

1470
01:04:11.240 --> 01:04:16.240
that really made the inside, it was like in the inside of your eye, reddish pink.

1471
01:04:16.540 --> 01:04:21.120
So my eyes looked the part, and then emotionally I got there.

1472
01:04:22.080 --> 01:04:25.760
Your eyes looked like you had three margaritas yesterday.

1473
01:04:27.020 --> 01:04:28.260
That's what you look like.

1474
01:04:28.260 --> 01:04:31.740
Actually, that should have been my prep instead of eyeliner and sad thoughts.

1475
01:04:32.620 --> 01:04:38.920
No, what happened was Laverne just showed Kenneth Paul a picture of me from the previous day

1476
01:04:38.920 --> 01:04:40.640
and was like, make her look like that.

1477
01:04:41.020 --> 01:04:45.740
No, but in all seriousness, Angela, when I was watching these series of scenes where your character

1478
01:04:45.740 --> 01:04:53.300
is really, really devastated over the death of Sprinkles, I was just so beyond impressed

1479
01:04:53.300 --> 01:04:58.000
with your performance and your range and your believability.

1480
01:04:58.440 --> 01:05:02.060
It was just, this is just great, great work.

1481
01:05:02.280 --> 01:05:03.220
Aw, thanks.

1482
01:05:03.300 --> 01:05:04.640
I appreciate that.

1483
01:05:04.860 --> 01:05:10.380
I really appreciated Greg writing the storyline for me, and I got to do all these things,

1484
01:05:10.480 --> 01:05:17.120
you know, and, you know, his take as a director was always to try to keep it as honest as possible.

1485
01:05:17.800 --> 01:05:18.460
Yeah.

1486
01:05:19.400 --> 01:05:20.000
Yeah.

1487
01:05:20.000 --> 01:05:26.900
Well, there's another really great moment in this scene, and we actually had a fan write in.

1488
01:05:27.120 --> 01:05:28.500
Katie Harwick said,

1489
01:05:28.500 --> 01:05:34.180
I think we need to give a shout-out to Michael when Angela's cat dies.

1490
01:05:34.600 --> 01:05:39.080
Not only did he know her name, but he was overcome with grief.

1491
01:05:39.240 --> 01:05:44.160
He cares so much for his employees, and it was just such a sweet moment to me.

1492
01:05:44.360 --> 01:05:51.220
But I do have to ask, do you think he was truly sad, or did he just see this as a distraction

1493
01:05:51.220 --> 01:05:54.000
from hitting Meredith that everyone could talk about instead?

1494
01:05:54.000 --> 01:05:58.820
Instead, I personally think he was very distraught about sprinkles.

1495
01:05:59.120 --> 01:06:00.160
Well, I agree.

1496
01:06:00.460 --> 01:06:06.380
This happens at 12 minutes, 41 seconds, and it is one of my favorite endearing moments of Michael.

1497
01:06:06.520 --> 01:06:10.540
Now, maybe because it's personal for me, because, you know, I played Angela Martin.

1498
01:06:10.640 --> 01:06:12.140
I knew how much she loved her cats.

1499
01:06:12.480 --> 01:06:18.680
But Michael, it's like that moment when the trick-or-treaters come to his house, and you see his joy.

1500
01:06:18.940 --> 01:06:22.700
It's like that moment when he shows up to Pam's art show.

1501
01:06:23.240 --> 01:06:23.680
Yeah.

1502
01:06:23.680 --> 01:06:27.280
Michael really saw these people as his family.

1503
01:06:27.540 --> 01:06:30.220
So Michael knew Angela's love of sprinkles.

1504
01:06:30.380 --> 01:06:31.280
Of course he did.

1505
01:06:31.720 --> 01:06:32.280
Yeah.

1506
01:06:32.280 --> 01:06:35.060
And he was gutted to hear that sprinkles died.

1507
01:06:35.240 --> 01:06:39.920
The way he puts his hand up to his face, and he kind of collapses into the wall, and he's like,

1508
01:06:40.480 --> 01:06:41.480
oh, shoot.

1509
01:06:41.880 --> 01:06:43.520
I'm sorry, Angela.

1510
01:06:43.940 --> 01:06:46.360
I mean, could it get any worse?

1511
01:06:47.060 --> 01:06:48.560
He's feeling all of that.

1512
01:06:48.740 --> 01:06:50.000
He really feels bad.

1513
01:06:50.000 --> 01:06:57.040
And now he gets sprinkles' name right the first time, and then he makes a big speech and calls her prinkles.

